TEST T33369 -- (210) Authentication&Security_TwoStepAuthentication - Mac-based 1st then 802.1x 2nd
================================================================================
Run:      2026-10-23 15:57-16:09 NZDT.  Two-step authentication was measured on the
          wire, in both configured orders, with four different outcomes.
          The DUT's clock reads UTC, 13 hours behind the NZDT times in this log.
Bench:    tb277, consoles u2 (swi_d); Test Engineer bidhanc@bidhanc-dl
Tester:   bench-runner
Graded:   tester
Case:     AWPTCM-T33369.  The test-case database holds no steps for this case.  The
          objective used was: show that MAC authentication must succeed first, and only
          then is 802.1X attempted.  A client that passes MAC but fails 802.1X must not
          be authorised.  A client that fails MAC must never reach 802.1X.  The product
          support list row 208 "Mac-based (1st) then 802.1x (2nd)" reads Yes.
