TOPOLOGY AS TESTED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  One port, two crafted client MACs, one at a time.  The DUT is both the authenticator
  and the RADIUS server, so no second switch and no external server took part.

        tb277  eth4   -- MAC C 02:0d:b9:00:33:69 and MAC D 02:0d:b9:00:33:6a
             |           EAPOL from tools/eapol.py, ARP from tools/arpleg.py
             |
             |  (down)  EAPOL frames and ARP requests
             |  (up)    EAP frames from the DUT, and ARP replies when authorised
             v
    +----------------------------------------------------+
    |  swi_d   AT-x960-56YSQ                   <-- DUT   |
    |  port1.0.48: auth-mac enable,                      |
    |              dot1x port-control auto,              |
    |              auth two-step enable,                 |
    |              auth two-step order <either way>      |
    |         |                                          |
    |         +--> radius-server local, 127.0.0.1        |
    +----------------------------------------------------+
             ^
             |  console, 115200 baud
        tb277  /dev/u2

  DUT     : swi_d (AT-x960-56YSQ) console u2 at 115200 baud, S/N A2WQS700B,
            software sin_x96056-20261019-27.  Not a stack.
  server  : the DUT's own local RADIUS server.  `radius-server local`, NAS 127.0.0.1,
            `aaa authentication dot1x default group radius`.  This case added
            `aaa authentication auth-mac default group radius` and the local user
            `02-0d-b9-00-33-69`, and removed both at the end.
  link    : tb277 eth4 <-> swi_d port1.0.48 (access port in vlan 48; the DUT's vlan 48
            address is 10.38.22.66/27, MAC e0:1a:ea:d4:70:43)
  clients : MAC C 02:0d:b9:00:33:69, sender IP 10.38.22.72.  It passes MAC
            authentication, because the user `02-0d-b9-00-33-69` was created.
            MAC D 02:0d:b9:00:33:6a, sender IP 10.38.22.73.  It fails MAC
            authentication, because no such user exists.  Its 802.1X credentials
            (`ckmulti1`) are deliberately valid, so that 802.1X would succeed if it
            were ever reached.
  probe   : the dataplane probe is 3 or 4 ARP requests for the DUT's own vlan 48
            address.  The measurement is how many ARP replies come back.
  tools   : tools/eapol.py and tools/arpleg.py on tb277; tools/tb ckcon for the
            console; tools/qmark.py for the read-only help probe; tools/tb health for
            the two health reads

  Every leg below was preceded by `dot1x initialize interface port1.0.48`.

