STEP B -- build the MAC-authentication half of the rig                       done
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Method: the port already did 802.1X.  Two-step also needs MAC authentication to work.
  Two facts had to be measured before any step could run.

  First, MAC authentication needs its own method list.  With only the 802.1X list
  configured, enabling `auth-mac enable` and sending a frame created a supplicant entry
  on the port but sent no RADIUS request at all.  `show radius local-server statistics`
  did not change and the DUT's log stayed empty.  The missing line is:

awplus(config)# aaa authentication auth-mac default group radius

  Second, the user name that MAC authentication sends was not guessed.  With the method
  list in place, one ARP frame from the new MAC made the DUT's own RADIUS server print
  the name it had tried:

awplus# show radius local-server statistics
Users NOT present in the User Database:
Username                               Successes  Failures  Last Interaction
02-0d-b9-00-33-69                              0         1  23 Oct 2026 03:00:37

  So the name is the MAC in lower case with hyphens.  It is also the password.  A local
  user `02-0d-b9-00-33-69` with password `02-0d-b9-00-33-69` was created and MAC
  authentication then worked at the first attempt.

