     0.003 02:0d:b9:00:33:6a -> EAPOL-Start        <-- never answered, in 45 seconds
  02:0d:b9:00:33:6a  expected success, got timeout -- MISMATCH
  RESULT T33369-S2-dot1x-NEVER-REACHED-valid-credentials: 0/1 matched -- MISMATCH

  => STEP 2 PASS.  The tool printed MISMATCH because the leg was declared
     `--expect success` on purpose, so that the instrument, and not the tester, would
     state the shortfall.  One EAPOL frame in 45 seconds.  The DUT never sent an
     EAP-Request/Identity, so 802.1X was not failed, it was never started.  The
     credentials behind it were good.  One field tells the two cases apart, read the same
     way in both: when the MAC step passes the supplicant reads `802.1X` and
     `PAE: Connecting`; when the MAC step fails it still reads
     `MAC-based Authentication` and `PAE: Held`.  The DUT never moves past step 1.

